ENGINEERING CONSTITUTION — ALPHA SWARM

─────────────────────────────────────────────────
DATA SOURCES
─────────────────────────────────────────────────
Fundamentals:
  - yfinance              : price, financials, balance sheet, cash flow (free tier)
  - sec-edgar-api         : 10-K, 10-Q, 13F filings, insider transactions
  - financial-modeling-prep (FMP) : historical metrics, DCF templates, peer comps
  - simfin                : standardised income statements (free tier available)

Macro:
  - FRED API (St. Louis Fed) : interest rates, CPI, PCE, unemployment, M2
  - BIS statistics           : global debt levels, credit-to-GDP gaps
  - OECD.stat                : leading indicators, composite PMIs

Sentiment / Positioning:
  - SEC EDGAR 13F filings    : institutional positioning (quarterly)
  - FINVIZ                   : short interest, insider trades
  - AAII sentiment survey    : retail investor sentiment (contrarian signal)

Alternative / Quality Checks:
  - Quandl / Nasdaq Data Link : commodity prices, alternative datasets
  - OpenCorporates            : corporate structure verification

─────────────────────────────────────────────────
ANALYSIS TOOLS  (Python stack)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────
tools/dcf_engine.py
  - Two-stage DCF with dynamic WACC (bottom-up beta + ERP)
  - Explicit forecast period: 5 years (conservative: analyst consensus −30%)
  - Terminal growth rate: max(2.5%, GDP_long_term_estimate) — never exceed 3%
  - Output: intrinsic_value, sensitivity_table (WACC ±1%, g ±0.5%)

tools/factor_scorer.py
  - VALUE    : composite(P/B, P/E, P/FCF, EV/EBITDA) → sector percentile
  - QUALITY  : ROIC trend, gross margin trend, accruals ratio, leverage trend
  - MOMENTUM : 12-1 month price return, earnings revision momentum (3m)
  - LOW_VOL  : 3y Sharpe ratio, max drawdown, beta vs. benchmark
  - Weights  : 40 / 30 / 20 / 10
  - Output   : composite_score /100

tools/beneish.py
  - Beneish M-Score (8 variables): DSRI, GMI, AQI, SGI, DEPI, SGAI, LVGI, TATA
  - Threshold: score > −1.78 → potential earnings manipulation → HARD REJECT

tools/kelly.py
  - Kelly fraction: f* = (p × b − q) / b
    p = P(price reaches intrinsic value within 3 years), estimated by analyst
    b = upside_to_IV / downside_to_bear_case
  - Default: half-Kelly (f* / 2) for prudence
  - Output: recommended_position_pct, max_position_pct (cap at 10%)

tools/altman.py
  - Altman Z-Score (Zones: > 2.99 safe, 1.23–2.99 grey, < 1.23 distress)
  - Threshold: score < 1.23 → HARD REJECT

─────────────────────────────────────────────────
OUTPUT FORMAT — INVESTMENT MEMO
─────────────────────────────────────────────────
All agents produce machine-readable JSON + human narrative.
JSON schema (saved to ./tmp/<ticker>-memo.json):
{
  "ticker":            string,
  "date":              ISO8601,
  "agent":             string,
  "intrinsic_value":   float | null,
  "current_price":     float | null,
  "margin_of_safety":  float | null,
  "moat_score":        int | null,
  "management_grade":  string | null,
  "factor_score":      int | null,
  "kelly_fraction":    float | null,
  "risk_score":        int | null,
  "conviction":        int | null,
  "scenarios": {
    "bull":  float,
    "base":  float,
    "bear":  float
  },
  "bias_checklist":    object,
  "red_flags":         array,
  "recommendation":    string,
  "verdict_narrative": string
}

─────────────────────────────────────────────────
QUALITY GATES  (hard blocks on handoff)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────
  [ ] intrinsic_value is populated (no handoff without a number)
  [ ] risk_score is populated
  [ ] All three scenarios (bull / base / bear) are populated
  [ ] All six bias checklist items are evaluated
  [ ] recommendation field is set
  [ ] Sources cited with timestamp for all financial data used
